[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: router16
diagnosis_text:
The outage is not caused by mswitch0. Its OSPF is up and advertising the Campus 1 SVIs, but it has no OSPF neighbor on the uplink subnet, so it learns no external routes.

Mechanism:
- On mswitch0, OSPF is enabled for 10.2.2.0/24 and the VLANs (10/20/30). “show ip ospf interface” shows br0 (10.2.2.2/24) in state DR with Neighbor Count 0, and “show ip ospf neighbor” is empty. Its routing table contains only connected networks, matching the symptom that inter-VLAN inside Campus 1 works while off-campus routes are missing.
- L2/L3 to the uplink is fine: mswitch0 can ping router16 at 10.2.2.1 with 0% loss, so the physical/logical uplink is not the issue.

Localization:
- The uplink adjacency should be between mswitch0 br0 (10.2.2.2) and router16 bond0 (10.2.2.1) over r16_ms0/r16_ms0_2. On router16, frr.service is failed and ospfd is not running; its running config contains no OSPF stanza, so it cannot form an adjacency with mswitch0.

Root cause: FRR/OSPF is down and misconfigured on router16 (no OSPF configuration present and service failed), breaking the OSPF adjacency on the 10.2.2.0/24 uplink.

Corrective fix:
- On router16, restore and enable OSPF: e.g., “router ospf; network 10.2.2.0/24 area 0; network 172.30.1.0/24 area 0”, ensure Router-ID is set or derived, then start frr.service. Verify mswitch0 br0 forms an OSPF neighbor with 10.2.2.1 and that external routes reappear on mswitch0. No changes are needed on mswitch0. 
=== END ===